  "question": {
    "text": "A uniform heavy rod of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>. Cross sectional area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math> and length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> is hanging from a fixed support. Neglecting the lateral contraction, the elongation in the rod due to its own weight is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _____ .<br />(Given. Young&#39;s modulus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>11</mn></msup><msup><mi>Nm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> )"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "25",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"assets\\st0050_3811a29cb708.png\" style=\"width: 90px; height: 144px;\" /></p><p>Tension at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> from lower end <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></mfrac><mi>x</mi></math></p><p>If the elongation in the element is taken as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>d</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;then, using Hooke&#39;s law,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>d</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>d</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>d</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>d</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>d</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>d</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>A</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>11</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
